  ('ent_anna-wintour', 'person', 'anna-wintour', 'Anna Wintour', 'published', 'Dame Anna Wintour (; born 3 November 1949) is a British and American media executive who served as editor-in-chief of Vogue from 1988 to 2025. Currently, Wintour serves as global chief content officer and artist director at Condé Nast. Known for her trademark pageboy bob haircut and dark sunglasses, Wintour is regarded as the most powerful woman in publishing, and has become an important figure in', '["src_wikidata"]', unixepoch(), 50, 'en');

