  ('ent_bess-truman', 'person', 'bess-truman', 'Bess Truman', 'published', 'Elizabeth Virginia Truman (née Wallace; February 13, 1885 – October 18, 1982) was First Lady of the United States from 1945 to 1953 as the wife of President Harry S. Truman. She had previously served as Second Lady of the United States from January to April 1945. At 97 years, 247 days, she was the longest-lived first and second spouse.', '["src_wikidata"]', unixepoch(), 50, 'en');

