  ('ent_dalai-lama', 'person', 'dalai-lama', 'Dalai Lama', 'published', 'The Dalai Lama (UK: , US: ; Tibetan: ཏཱ་ལའི་བླ་མ་, Wylie: Tā la''i bla ma [táːlɛː láma]) is the spiritual head  of Tibetan Buddhism. The term is part of the full title "Holiness Knowing Everything Vajradhara Dalai Lama" given by Altan Khan. He offered it in appreciation to the Gelug school''s then-leader, Sonam Gyatso, who received the title in 1578 at Yanghua Monastery. At that time, Sonam Gyatso h', '["src_wikidata"]', unixepoch(), 50, 'en');

