  ('ent_dierks-bentley', 'person', 'dierks-bentley', 'Dierks Bentley', 'published', 'Frederick Dierks Bentley (; born November 20, 1975) is an American country singer and songwriter. Bentley moved to Nashville in the late 90s to pursue a career in music, leading up to his releasing the self-funded and independent album Don''t Leave Me in Love in 2001. In 2003, he signed to Capitol Nashville and released his eponymous debut album. Both it and its follow-up, 2005''s Modern Day Drifter', '["src_wikidata"]', unixepoch(), 50, 'en');

