  ('ent_george-westinghouse', 'person', 'george-westinghouse', 'George Westinghouse', 'published', 'George Westinghouse Jr. (October 6, 1846 – March 12, 1914) was a prolific American inventor, engineer, and entrepreneurial industrialist based in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. He is best known for his creation of the railway air brake and for being a pioneer in the development and use of alternating current (AC) electrical power distribution. During his career, he received 360 patents for his inventio', '["src_wikidata"]', unixepoch(), 50, 'en');

