  ('ent_jesse-jackson', 'person', 'jesse-jackson', 'Jesse Jackson', 'published', 'Jesse Louis Jackson (né Burns; October 8, 1941 – February 17, 2026) was an American civil rights activist, LGBTQ rights activist, politician, and ordained Baptist minister. A protégé of Martin Luther King Jr. and James Bevel during the civil rights movement, he became one of the most prominent civil rights leaders of the late 20th and early 21st centuries, and an ardent advocate and early supporte', '["src_wikidata"]', unixepoch(), 50, 'en');

