  ('cs_joe-gebbia_intro', 'ent_joe-gebbia', 'biography_intro', 'Introduction', 'Joseph Gebbia Jr. (; born August 21, 1981) is an American designer and entrepreneur, and a co-founder of Airbnb. In 2025, he joined the Department of Government Efficiency (DOGE). Gebbia was appointed by President Donald Trump as the first Chief Design Officer to lead the National Design Studio.
