  ('ent_julia-tyler', 'person', 'julia-tyler', 'Julia Gardiner Tyler', 'published', 'Julia Gardiner Tyler (May 4, 1820 – July 10, 1889) was the first lady of the United States from June 26, 1844, to March 4, 1845, as the second wife of President John Tyler. A member of the influential Gardiner family, Tyler had many figures as suitors. She met the widowed President Tyler in 1842, and agreed to marry him after he comforted her in the aftermath of her father David Gardiner''s death. ', '["src_wikidata"]', unixepoch(), 50, 'en');

