VALUES
  ('ent_ken-thompson', 'person', 'ken-thompson', 'Ken Thompson', 'published', 'Kenneth Lane Thompson (born February 4, 1943) is an American pioneer of computer science. Thompson worked at Bell Labs for most of his career where he designed and implemented the original Unix operating system. He also invented the B programming language, the direct predecessor to the C language, and was one of the creators and early developers of the Plan 9 operating system. Other notable contri', '["src_wikidata"]', unixepoch(), 50, 'en');

